    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a756307_737022b9",
        "filename": "libsepol/cil/src/android.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 919,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003966
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-15T01:04:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be better if this was a boolean, rather than an int.\n\nThe return value is confusing... Sometimes you return SEPOL_ERR (for instance, line 921), and sometimes you return -1 (line 942). However, SEPOL_ERR and -1 are both the same, so I\u0027m not sure what I\u0027m suppose to make of this. Similarly, SEPOL_OK is returned sometimes, and 0 is returned sometimes, but they\u0027re both the same value.\n\nIt feels like you really want to return a boolean here, or have an enum of possible values, but mixing different types of return values is confusing...",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 919,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 919,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "3129eadf5c9de09b878816ad6525b14881223b9a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a756307_e26196bb",
        "filename": "libsepol/cil/src/android.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 919,
      "author": {
        "id": 1026058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-15T23:23:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree the mixing is undesirable.  I\u0027d like to keep this consistent with the rest of the cil code for now, though, so I\u0027ll convert the ints to SEPOL_OK and SEPOL_ERR, which could easily be moved to a bool if desired, but right now there are no cil (or libsepol) bool interfaces, so it would change the expectations of the calling code.  This also enables additional error codes exposed by the inner libsepol calls, e.g. cil_compile to be propogated as is expected in the rest of the code, in case they differ from plain SEPOL_ERR.",
      "parentUuid": "1a756307_737022b9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 919,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 919,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "3129eadf5c9de09b878816ad6525b14881223b9a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
